ing  blow as superman pushes the alien menace  back toward the portal  that will bring him back to dark side  diana jumps in with a sword slicing his  head off just before he enters the boom  tube  this was the intended ending to justice  league all along  and it's one of the reasons that fans  are loving this restored version of the  character  one user posted on twitter this is  easily the best movie that has ever been  made  about wonder woman her personality  culture family  ability strength wisdom etc she carries  the action in the film  and they give her a ton of screen time  to showcase her power  in a way i've never seen anyone do  before a scene allows diana to exhibit  her fierceness and boldness as a warrior  removing any doubt about her abilities  and bringing back a vision of the  character that should have never been  allowed to lapse as it did in the  original justice league there's no doubt  that steppenwolf is a powerful foe  requiring the combined efforts of heroes  like superman and the wonder woman  despite their own formidable strengths  in dc comics canon steppenwolf is a new  god  diana is a demigod her father was zeus  and her mother was hippolyta of the  amazons  in this way they are equals this means  that to director zack snyder wonder  woman killing steppenwolf is basically  the only ending that makes any sense by  definition gods can't be killed  at least not by mere mortals even ones  with mutant powers like aquaman or ones  who get theirs from the yellow sun like  superman  in 2019 snyder made a post on vero that  revealed his concept of that climactic  scene in three unfinished images  in the caption he noted not sure how  they killed steppenwolf in the  theatrical version of justice  league this was never finished all the  way but i used gods to kill gods  it turns out snyder's idea of wonder  woman seems so reasonable  that it's the one many others are  embracing too  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more loo